# Project: Facility Ops Agent

A chat agent + dashboard that tracks and manages facility/operations records for a single site (one office/building). It replaces scattered spreadsheets and manual logs with a single source of truth that can be queried and updated either through a web dashboard or by chatting with the agent.

## Tracked domains (current scope)
Priority is inherited from the source register and drives build order.

| # | Domain | Format (source) | Priority |
|---|--------|------------------|----------|
| 8 | Kitchen inventory list & reorder levels | Excel | High |
| 9 | IT equipment register | Excel | High |
| 10 | Generator maintenance schedule & fuel log | Excel | High |
| 11 | Solar system specs & monitoring requirements | Word / PDF | High |
| 12 | Internet & utility account details | Excel | Medium |
| 13 | Tenants (accounts, rent logs, electricity bills) | Dashboard / chat | Medium |

More domains (items 1–7) may be added later — every new domain must follow the same table + CRUD + agent-tool pattern already established, not a one-off structure.

## Core principle
The chat agent is a thin conversational layer over the dashboard's data layer. It never writes directly to the database with ad-hoc queries — it only calls the same typed functions/API routes the dashboard UI uses. This keeps both surfaces consistent and auditable.

## Build discipline
This project is built in explicit phases (see `040-build-phases.mdc`). Do not implement a later phase's functionality while working on an earlier one, even if it looks like a quick win. Flag it and move on when the current phase is done.
